<title>HUNGARY: Hungary 2-yr bond yield remains steady at 18.81pct.</title>
<headline>Hungary 2-yr bond yield remains steady at 18.81pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Hungary's two-year government bonds of 199/F series was set at 18.81 percent at an auction on Thursday, unchanged from an auction held one month ago, the Government Debt Management Agency (AKK) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>    First day of interest period     3 March 1997</p>
<p>    Date of maturity		    12 April 1999</p>
<p>    Bonds on offer			20,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total bids			    27,907.20 million forints</p>
<p>    Total allocated		     20,000</p>
<p>    Total issued			  22,000</p>
<p>    Average net price			 97.52 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield			     18.81 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: The bond bears a fixed interest rate of 16.5 percent, payable semi- anually starting from October 12, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
</text>
